This directory contains the source code for third-party libraries
vendored by RT. The contents below are generated from the per-library
metadata.yml files; see SCHEMA.md for the field reference. Do not edit
this file by hand -- run devel/tools/generate-third-party-readme --write
to regenerate.

* bootstrap/ (4.6.1)
Description: Front-end framework for building responsive, mobile-first web
  sites.
Origin: https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap
License: MIT

* bootstrap-combobox/ (1.2.0)
Description: Combobox widget for Bootstrap, adding autocomplete behavior to
  <select>.
Origin: https://github.com/danielfarrell/bootstrap-combobox
License: Apache-2.0
Note:
  The scoped npm package @danielfarrell/bootstrap-combobox stops at 1.1.8;
  the 1.2.0 we ship corresponds to the upstream GitHub release tag of the
  same number and was never published to npm. The purl uses the GitHub
  form so advisory lookups resolve against the actual artifact we ship.

* bootstrap-icons/ (1.10.3)
Description: Official open source SVG icon library for Bootstrap with over
  1,900 icons.
Origin: https://github.com/twbs/icons
License: MIT
Note:
  Unlike the other entries under devel/third-party/, this directory holds
  only metadata. The icons themselves are individual SVG files under
  share/static/images/, selected per %SVG in etc/RT_Config.pm.in.

* bootstrap-select/ (1.13.18)
Description: Enhanced <select> widget for Bootstrap with search, multi-select,
  and styling options.
Origin: https://github.com/snapappointments/bootstrap-select
License: MIT

* chart-js-2/ (2.9.4)
Description: HTML5 charts using the <canvas> tag.
Origin: https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js
License: MIT

* chartjs-plugin-colorschemes/ (0.3.0)
Description: Predefined color schemes for Chart.js.
Origin: https://github.com/nagix/chartjs-plugin-colorschemes
License: MIT
Note:
  This is the original nagix project, no longer actively maintained.
  The current maintained fork lives at MaximBelov/chartjs-plugin-colorschemes
  and is published on npm as hw-chartjs-plugin-colorschemes; RT 5 has not
  migrated to it.

* chosen/ (1.4.2)
Description: Replaces native <select> elements with a more user-friendly
  autocomplete dropdown.
Origin: https://github.com/harvesthq/chosen
License: MIT
Note:
  The npm package name is `chosen-js`; the bare `chosen` name on npm
  belongs to an unrelated package.

* ckeditor4/ (4.20.1)
Description: WYSIWYG rich-text editor (version 4 series). Parses and renders
  user-supplied HTML, so any vulnerability here is a direct XSS exposure in
  RT's ticket UI.
Origin: https://github.com/ckeditor/ckeditor4
License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Note:
  CKEditor 4 is in extended-support mode upstream; CKEditor 5 ships in
  RT 6.0 and onward, while RT 5 stays on the 4.x line. The directory
  holds both COPYING.GPL (the operative GPL v2 license text RT uses) and
  LICENSE.md (the upstream summary describing the GPL/LGPL/MPL choice
  alongside the commercial alternative).

* clipboard/ (2.0.8)
Description: Lightweight library for copying text to the clipboard via
  JavaScript.
Origin: https://github.com/zenorocha/clipboard.js
License: MIT
Note:
  Single-file library: the upstream source clipboard-2.0.8.js lives in
  this directory; the minified copy shipped to clients lives separately
  under share/static/js/.
  The banner inside clipboard-2.0.8.js says "clipboard.js v2.0.6" even
  at the upstream v2.0.8 release tag -- upstream cut the v2.0.8 release
  without bumping the in-file version string. The 2.0.8 recorded here
  tracks the upstream release tag, which is what advisory databases
  reference.

* d3/ (5.15.1)
Description: Data-Driven Documents -- library for producing dynamic,
  interactive data visualizations using SVG, Canvas and HTML.
Origin: https://github.com/d3/d3
License: BSD-3-Clause

* dropzone-4/ (4.0.1)
Description: Drag-and-drop file upload widget. Handles user-provided files,
  making it a security-relevant entry point.
Origin: https://github.com/enyo/dropzone
License: MIT
Note:
  This is the original enyo/dropzone project, now inactive. A
  maintained fork lives at NicolasCARPi/dropzone and is published as
  @deltablot/dropzone on npm; RT 5 has not migrated to it.

* eyedropper.svg
Description: Color picker icon.
Origin: https://thenounproject.com/noun/eye-dropper/
Author: The Noun Project
License: CC BY 3.0

* fontawesome/ (5.15.4)
Description: Icon library. RT vendors the free SVG icons plus
  webpack-generated JavaScript covering only the icons the application
  actually uses.
Origin: https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome
License: MIT
Note:
  Font Awesome Free is multi-licensed: code under MIT, icons under
  CC BY 4.0, and fonts under SIL OFL 1.1. The SPDX is set to the code
  portion (MIT) since the JavaScript we ship is what carries any CVE
  surface; icon-asset usage requires CC BY 4.0 attribution per upstream
  terms. See LICENSE.txt for the full multi-license summary.

* jquery/ (3.6.0)
Description: DOM manipulation, event handling, and AJAX helpers. Foundational
  JS dependency used throughout RT's UI.
Origin: https://github.com/jquery/jquery
License: MIT
Note:
  Single-file library: the upstream source jquery-3.6.0.js lives in this
  directory; the minified copy shipped to clients lives separately under
  share/static/js/.

* jquery-jgrowl/ (1.4.5)
Description: JavaScript notification system providing growl-style messages.
Origin: https://github.com/stanlemon/jGrowl
License: MIT

* jquery-tablesorter/ (2.0.5b)
Description: Client-side sortable HTML tables without page refresh.
Origin: https://github.com/christianbach/tablesorter
License: MIT
Note:
  Single-file library. The original project (christianbach) is no longer
  actively maintained; the Mottie/tablesorter fork is the current home of
  this code on npm but RT has not migrated to it.
  Upstream ships no standalone LICENSE file; the file in this directory
  was reconstructed from the source-file header in jquery.tablesorter.js,
  which declares: "Copyright (c) 2007 Christian Bach. Dual licensed under
  the MIT and GPL licenses." RT uses this code under the MIT half of that
  offer (SPDX: MIT).

* jquery-ui/ (1.13.2)
Description: Curated set of user-interface widgets and interactions built on
  jQuery.
Origin: https://github.com/jquery/jquery-ui
License: MIT
Note:
  This bundle was produced from jQuery UI's downloadable component builder
  (https://jqueryui.com/download/), which generates customized JS/CSS
  containing only the selected widgets. The original directory name was
  jquery-ui-1.13.2.custom; the ".custom" marker is recorded here since
  the directory has since been renamed.

* mousetrap/ (1.5.3)
Description: Library for binding keyboard shortcuts.
Origin: https://github.com/ccampbell/mousetrap
License: Apache-2.0
Note:
  Single-file library. The upstream project has been minimally maintained
  for years; consider auditing for an actively-maintained alternative if
  a CVE lands.

* selectize/ (0.12.6)
Description: Hybrid combo-box and autocomplete widget with tagging, remote
  data, and create-on-the-fly options.
Origin: https://github.com/selectize/selectize.js
License: Apache-2.0

* superfish/ (1.7.10)
Description: Enhanced Suckerfish-style menu plugin for jQuery.
Origin: https://github.com/joeldbirch/superfish
License: MIT
Note:
  The vendored superfish.js source-file header declares dual MIT/GPL
  licensing; upstream's repo currently ships only MIT-LICENSE.txt. SPDX
  is set to MIT because we use the MIT half of the dual offer.
  The purl uses the github form because superfish has had inconsistent
  npm publishing history; the github purl resolves against the actual
  shipped artifact more reliably than guessing at an npm package name.
